1|0@texas^1440374172#cudbyiq:JayRoth22$:It normally is but of course the day we went it stopped being 100 degrees and rained on us pretty hard. We still managed to catch a few nice sized largemouth. Theres plenty of coves and brush piles to hit as you make your way down the lake.
2|0@texas^1440376020#cudd5ei:Dekire$:We're you fishing from the shore? What kind of lures? New to bass fishing and come through austin sometimes
1|0@texas^1440377286#cuddwoj:JayRoth22$:We were fishing from a boat. We launched from the 360 bridge. There is a fee to use their ramps since its government owned. And I was using a simple texas rig (plenty of youtube videos explaining how to rig). It works really well. Its the best to help you not get cought in those brush piles. Jigging the bait worked well that day but swimming it back is always good to try.
